// A test source without phase drift : the sine of an integer phase.
// os.osc accumulates a real phase, whose rounding drifts in single precision : after one
// second the float and double renders are out of phase, and only their levels compare.
// Here the phase is an integer counter modulo N = 2^22, exact in float and in double
// (m < 2^24), so both renders read the same phase at every sample ; they differ only by
// the rounding of 2*pi and of sin, bounded, never accumulated. The frequency is rounded
// to a multiple of SR/N (the step k is checked to be the same integer in both precisions
// for every frequency the tests use, at the six rates of check_precision.py).
toscN = 4194304;
toscStep(f) = int(float(f) * toscN / library("maths.lib").SR + 0.5);  // float(f) : f * toscN in int overflows above 512 Hz
tosc(f) = sin(2.0 * library("maths.lib").PI * float(m) / toscN)
with {
    m = (+(toscStep(f)) : %(toscN)) ~ _;
};
